.SH NAME
gmc-wt-add - Create new worktrees with new branches


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgmc wt add [name...] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Create one or more worktrees, each on a new branch named after its directory.
With -b and no name, the worktree name is derived from the base branch.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-b\fP, \fB--base\fP=""
	Base branch to create from

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for add

.PP
\fB--pr\fP=0
	Create a worktree from a pull request

.PP
\fB--sync\fP[=false]
	Sync base branch before creating worktree


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	Config file (default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/gmc/config.yaml)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug output

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="text"
	Output format: text or json


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  gmc wt add feature-login
  gmc wt add -b feat/existing-branch
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgmc-wt(1)\fP


